# Copy to .env.local for a build that should read imagery from somewhere other than
# this origin's /tiles. Leave it unset (or empty) for the local-first default, which is
# what every checkout of this repo uses: the pyramid is baked into the gitignored
# public/tiles/ and served from the same origin.
#
# Accepted values: a root-relative path, or an https:// URL. Anything else -- including
# http://, which a browser would block as mixed content -- is ignored with a warning at
# load, and the app falls back to /tiles. See docs/deploy.md for what the store has to
# send (Access-Control-Allow-Origin, and long Cache-Control).
NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_BASE_URL=
